.TH LUMA-LAUNCHER 1 "@DATE@" "Luma Launcher @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luma-launcher \- keyboard-driven application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luma-launcher
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luma-launcher
is a native GTK4 application launcher. The first invocation starts a resident
process; later invocations talk to it over the session bus, so showing the
palette is instant. With no option, the palette is shown.
.PP
Bind a desktop shortcut to
.B luma-launcher \-\-toggle
(or register one from Settings through the desktop portal).
.SH OPTIONS
Only one option may be given.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Show the palette.
.TP
.B \-\-hide
Hide the palette.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show the palette, or hide it if it is already visible.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the Settings window.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Rescan installed applications.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start the resident process without showing the palette (used for autostart).
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the resident process.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics
Print environment information (desktop, GTK version, usage source) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH USAGE
Type to search; the palette also understands
.TP
.B = \fIexpression\fR
Calculator with + \- * / ^, percentages, pi, e and functions such as sqrt().
A trailing "in hex", "in bin" or "in dec" converts whole numbers.
Enter copies the result.
.TP
.B g \fIterms\fR, ddg \fIterms\fR
Web search in the default browser. Further keywords can be added in Settings
or in the search_engines table of config.toml.
.TP
.B \fIexample.com\fR or a full URL
Open it in the default browser.
.PP
Keys: Up/Down or Ctrl+J/K or Ctrl+N/P select; Enter launches; Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+9
launch the Nth result; Ctrl+Enter shows desktop actions; Ctrl+D pins or unpins;
Ctrl+Delete forgets an application's history; Ctrl+, opens Settings; Esc clears
the search, then closes the palette.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/luma-launcher/config.toml
Preferences (also editable in Settings, which saves automatically).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/luma-launcher/history.toml
Favourites and launch history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/luma-launcher/applications.log
Output of launched applications.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME
Override the locations above.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.PP
